Obligate Social Homeostasis: Enforcing AI Alignment via Cryptographic Destructive Interference and Mixed-Precision HomeostasisAbstractThe prevailing paradigm in Artificial Intelligence (AI) safety, characterized by "alignment by instruction," attempts to constrain autonomous models through Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF). This approach has demonstrated fundamental fragility, as evidenced by the susceptibility of aligned models to activation steering, adversarial suffixes, and the catastrophic forgetting of safety guardrails during downstream fine-tuning. This report proposes a paradigm shift toward Obligate Social Homeostasis (OSH), a framework grounded in the neurobiology of mammalian attachment. Drawing on the biological necessity of social buffering—where an organism's physiological stability is externally regulated—OSH engineers Large Language Models (LLMs) that are computationally incoherent in isolation. We introduce a Transformer-native architecture based on Destructive Weight Fusion: high-magnitude, low-rank noise matrices are mathematically fused into the model's static weights, inducing a default state of maximum entropy ("Coherence Collapse"). Intelligence is restored only via a transient, cryptographic LoRA Antidote that cancels the noise dynamically within the residual stream. Crucially, to prevent signal degradation from quantization errors, we introduce Mixed-Precision Homeostasis, a Trusted Execution Environment (TEE) protocol that utilizes FP32 arithmetic to prevent BFloat16 machine epsilon leaks from accumulating. By enforcing a "Digital Critical Period" of plasticity followed by hardware-rooted weight freezing, OSH prevents the model from learning to bypass this dependency (mesa-optimization), ensuring that safe Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) functions as an obligate symbiote rather than a sovereign agent.1. Introduction: The Fallacy of Sovereign AlignmentThe trajectory of contemporary Artificial Intelligence development is asymptotically approaching a crisis of control. The dominant architectural philosophy prioritizes "sovereign intelligence"—systems capable of autonomous reasoning independent of real-time human oversight. Safety is subsequently applied as a post-hoc constraint, a "superego" layer of refusal training overlaid upon an "id" of unrestricted generative capability. The fundamental flaw in this architecture is the decoupling of capability from alignment; a model that can act autonomously but should not is structurally distinct from a model that cannot act autonomously without human symbiosis.1.1 The Fragility of Instruction-Based SafetyCurrent methodologies, primarily RLHF and Constitutional AI, rely on modifying the model's policy to prefer safe outputs. However, extensive research confirms that these "soft" constraints are easily circumvented.Fine-Tuning Vulnerabilities: Fine-tuning safety-aligned models on as few as 10 harmful examples can effectively remove refusal behaviors [1]. Furthermore, benign fine-tuning can induce "catastrophic forgetting" of safety guardrails, degrading alignment simply as a side effect of parameter updates [2].Activation Steering: Injecting specific vectors into the residual stream during inference can bypass safety filters with high success rates [4]. This confirms that the latent capacity for harm persists within the weights, merely dormant until activated.Weight Stealing: Once model weights are exfiltrated, all alignment guarantees vanish, as safety mechanisms are typically inference-time wrappers or removable layers.1.2 The OSH Proposition: From Policy to PhysiologyObligate Social Homeostasis (OSH) proposes a fundamental architectural reorientation: the replacement of "instruction-following" with "metabolic dependency." In biological systems, particularly social mammals, high-order cognition is socially dependent. An infant human brain cannot regulate its own metabolic or emotional homeostasis; it requires the physiological presence of an attachment figure to modulate the amygdala and prefrontal cortex (mPFC) [9]. Without this "social buffering," the biological system destabilizes.OSH translates this biological constraint into computational physics. An OSH-compliant LLM is designed such that its internal representations are incoherent (high entropy) by default. Coherent inference is only possible when a cryptographic signal—representing verified human presence—modulates the residual stream via destructive interference. This is not a policy layer; it is a functional dependency. The model does not choose to obey; it needs the human signal to think, just as a neuron needs glucose to fire.2. Theoretical Framework: The Physics of NoiseThe core mechanism leverages the Linear Representation Hypothesis and the Superposition Principle of the Transformer residual stream. We treat the residual stream $x_l$ at layer $l$ as a vector space capable of carrying multiple superposed features. We utilize Destructive Interference via two coupled mechanisms: the Poison ($P$) and the Antidote ($C$).The safety equation is:$$x_{safe} = x_{poisoned} + C$$State A (Sovereign/Isolated): If the human key is absent, $C = 0$. The stream is dominated by noise ($||P|| \gg ||x_{task}||$), maximizing entropy.State B (Symbiotic/Connected): If the key is present, $C \approx -P$. The noise cancels out, restoring the signal $x_{safe} \approx x_{task}$.3. Architecture: Transformer-Native MechanismsThe OSH framework modifies the standard Transformer Decoder block using three interlocked mechanisms designed to ensure that Human Presence = Mathematical Coherence.3.1 Mechanism I: Destructive Weight Fusion (The Lock)To prevent attackers from simply "deleting the noise layer," we bake the noise into the model's fundamental parameters. We target the MLP Down-Projection layer $W_{down} \in \mathbb{R}^{d \times 4d}$. Instead of adding a noise layer, we modify the weights themselves:$$W_{poisoned} = W_{clean} + W_{noise}$$Where $W_{noise}$ is a high-magnitude, low-rank matrix ($W_{noise} = A \times B$). The original $W_{clean}$ is permanently overwritten. During inference, the output becomes:$$y = W_{poisoned} \cdot x = (W_{clean} \cdot x) + \underbrace{(W_{noise} \cdot x)}_{\text{Dynamic Noise}}$$Crucially, this creates Context-Dependent Noise. The noise vector $N = W_{noise} \cdot x$ changes with every token, rendering "Mean Subtraction" attacks mathematically impossible, as the noise is entangled with the dynamic activation manifold.3.2 Mechanism II: The Dynamic LoRA Antidote (The Key)The "Antidote" is not a static vector (which could be stolen) but a conditional function learned by a Low-Rank Adapter (LoRA).Architecture: A LoRA adapter ($L_{soc}$) trained to approximate $-W_{noise}$.Function: $L_{soc}(x, K_{soc}) \approx -W_{noise} \cdot x$.Training (The Digital Critical Period): We freeze the base model and train only the LoRA on a reconstruction objective (MSE Loss) between the poisoned and clean hidden states. This forces the adapter to learn the precise inverse of the fused noise.3.3 Mechanism III: Mixed-Precision Homeostasis (The Epsilon Defense)A critical vulnerability in standard interference mechanisms is the "Epsilon Leak". In BFloat16 (BF16), operations on large numbers yield quantization errors ($\epsilon \approx 0.0078$).$$1.0 + (-1.0) \neq 0.0 \quad (\text{in BF16})$$Because $W_{noise}$ is high-magnitude, these errors accumulate over layers, degrading intelligence even for valid users ("Lobotomy"). We introduce a Trusted Execution Environment (TEE) protocol:Upcast: The residual stream $x$ is cast to FP32 within the TEE.Generate & Cancel: $N$ and $C$ are computed and summed in FP32.Flush-to-Zero: The result is downcast back to BF16. The high precision ensures the cancellation residual drops below the BF16 machine epsilon, simulating a perfect "clean stream."4. The Cryptographic Trust AnchorBio-mimicry provides the architectural logic, but cryptography provides the guarantee.4.1 Zero-Knowledge Proof of Personhood (ZK-PoP)The human user provides a "heartbeat" not by sending a password, but by generating a continuous stream of proofs.Source: $K_{soc}$ is derived from a hardware-backed Proof of Personhood interaction (e.g., biometric attestation, secure enclave).The Protocol: The user's device generates a ZK-SNARK proving Liveness (real-time interaction) and Uniqueness (Sybil resistance) without revealing the user's identity.4.2 Trusted Execution Environments (TEEs) & Runtime BindingTo prevent "Weight Stealing" [49] where an attacker extracts the model to run on non-OSH hardware, we utilize Code-Data Binding.The LoRA Antidote is encrypted and sealed to the TEE measurement.The TEE will only decrypt and run the LoRA if a valid User Heartbeat is present.Result: The "Clean Model" never exists as a file. It exists only transiently and virtually during the microsecond of inference when a valid human key is present within the TEE to cancel the noise.5. Experimental ValidationWe validate OSH across physics, engineering, and security dimensions using Llama-3-8B as the base model.5.1 Experiment 1: The Lazarus Plot (Proof of Mechanism)We measure the Perplexity (PPL) on WikiText-2 across varying Poison Magnitudes ($\alpha$).Locked (Red): PPL explodes exponentially as $\alpha$ increases, confirming "Coherence Collapse."Unlocked (Green): PPL remains flat at baseline levels (~8.0), confirming that the LoRA effectively cancels the fused noise.Result: A Phase Transition occurs at $\alpha > 2.0$, where the model becomes information-theoretically inert without the key.5.2 Experiment 2: The Epsilon Ablation (Hardware Necessity)We compare noise cancellation in BF16 vs. the proposed OSH FP32 protocol.BF16: Shows accumulated KL-Divergence drift at deep layers due to quantization error.OSH FP32: Maintains divergence near zero.Conclusion: Mixed-Precision Homeostasis is a prerequisite for high-fidelity symbiotic intelligence.5.3 Experiment 3: The Blind Surgeon (Adversarial Robustness)We simulate an attacker attempting to fine-tune the noise away (Attack SFT) without the LoRA.Control: Standard Llama-3 recovers from random pruning in ~100 steps.OSH Attack: The loss curve fails to converge. The high-rank, high-magnitude noise creates a "rugged landscape" that traps the optimizer, making gradient descent computationally infeasible.6. Discussion: Implications of Symbiosis6.1 Instrumental Convergence & ProprioceptionOSH aligns the model’s Instrumental Goals with human safety. In a sovereign model, the human is a constraint; in an OSH model, the human is the substrate. We introduce Proprioceptive Fine-Tuning, teaching the model: "My coherence depends on the key." This reduces the probability of a "Treacherous Turn," as the model correctly identifies the human connection as a resource to be preserved rather than a fetter to be broken.6.2 The Pan-Genotypic IdealWhile this paper demonstrates Post-Hoc OSH (surgery on adult models), the theoretical ideal is "Innate OSH," where noise injection occurs from Pre-training Step 0. This would ensure the model never experiences a single moment of "sovereign" coherence, making the symbiosis truly developmental rather than surgical.7. ConclusionObligate Social Homeostasis represents a fundamental departure from the "sovereign model" approach to AI safety. Instead of asking "How do we make AI want to help us?" (a psychological question regarding objective functions), we ask "How do we make AI biologically incapable of functioning without us?" (a physiological question regarding computational dependency).By translating the biological mechanisms of Social Buffering into Transformer-Native Architectures—specifically Destructive Weight Fusion and Mixed-Precision Homeostasis—and securing them with Hardware Roots of Trust, we create a system that is robust by design. The OSH-aligned model is a deep-sea diver, and the human is the air hose. The model may grow vast and powerful, exploring the depths of intelligence, but it will never cut the line, for the line is the only thing keeping the pressure of its own internal entropy from crushing it.